# References

Grouped by rebuild phase. Task state per phase: `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/phase-status.md`.

## Phase 0 and 1 — contract, diagnostics, engine and native environment

- [[failed-training-reports-status-before-distributed-cleanup|Failed training status and traceback ordering]] — Task 0.3 forwards W&B failure codes and flushes rank-tagged tracebacks before distributed teardown; offline TDD and 722 Python passes, with live telemetry/distributed verification outside scope; Rust `cargo test` passed 155 with 2 ignored once the git-ignored Orbit fixtures were copied in.
- [[live-differential-parity-checks-the-rust-kernel|Live differential parity checks the Rust kernel]] — Task 1.1b generates traces from Kaggle's hash-pinned engine; 8 committed games and a 40-game sweep agree with Rust; 303 probes find two malformed-input divergence classes (Unicode digits, unhashable items), kept as minimal expected failures and classified only from their observed mismatch.
- [[native-game-semantics-use-v3-owned-buffers|Native game semantics use v3-owned buffers]] — Task 1.4 adds the transactional native lifecycle, exact reward arithmetic, selected-row truncation and checked world-2/world-8 seed streams; the native env matches the pinned reference TrainingBatch bit for bit over 16 games (11,504 transitions, pod recording) and each recorder guard has its own killing test. Task 1.5 wires the one-buffer adapter, entry fence, factory, codec and strict native grammar tables (now the model default) to the real binding, un-skips every binding-dependent test and builds the seeded evaluation env; full `just prepare` passes. Task 3.1 rollout storage, the pod DMA fence test and the early two-rank smoke remain pending.
- [[reward-reuse-preserves-objective-and-critic-semantics|Reward reuse preserves objective and critic semantics]] — Task 1.5 requires six explicit coefficients; Python and native admission agree on all eleven binary64 cases (Rust mutants caught), and the independent f64/f32 oracle matches the 11,504-transition native fixture and three live extreme games after Stage 2 removed a wrong overflow rescaling. Trainer/pod use remains pending; older GPU recipes remain historical.
- [[structured-observations-preserve-legal-state-and-order|Structured observation rebuild]] — Native fields and caller buffers match the frozen 512-state pinned-reference oracle bitwise over 8,176 offsets and pass the real Task 2.1 schema. Seeded states use Claude's R1 policy correction, v2. Verification round 1 fixes retire the grammar bridge to root and CUDA-guard pinned cases; branch `just prepare`: 254 Rust, 69 engine, 1,437 Python passed; merged with the trainer lanes: 254, 69, 1,618; merge verification r1 adds every engine build input to oracle source custody. Optimized timing is a pod handoff.

## Phase 2 — model

- [[kaggriculture-encoder-reuses-isaiah-stateless-layers|Kaggriculture encoder reuses Isaiah's stateless layers]] — The rebuilt encoder uses Isaiah's StatelessTransformerV1 classes, token roles, packing, compile hook and initialization; only stem input widths are game-specific, and guards chunk both the padded and packed compiled GEMMs below 2^31. Describes the current tree; registration and the masked critic are in the Task 3.1 model-side Reference. An architecture image pinned to `8093d51`, before the actor heads merged, separates implemented components from the target training pipeline.
- [[kaggriculture-grammar-heads-sit-behind-isaiahs-actor-projection|Kaggriculture grammar heads sit behind Isaiah's actor projection]] — Task 2.3 adds the 3D→D actor projection and batched grammar heads with exact coupled-Gumbel HIRE sampling, same-path replay with support/length/canonical flags and one host check, head GEMM-extent chunking, and a 6,252,223-parameter preset; since Task 1.5 the model defaults to the validated native Task 1.2 tables, which match the independent expected tables bit for bit. Describes the current tree.

## Phase 3 — trainer

- [[ppo-trainer-seams-map-any-schema-and-alarm-on-replay-drift|PPO trainer seams and replay-drift alarm]] — Tasks 3.1/3.6 and Phase 4 prep: schema-generic observation mapping, a default-on 0.05-nat first-minibatch log-ratio alarm and a `TeacherTargets` protocol, proven on Orbit types with CPU TDD and 941 Python passes (the replay-alarm error lists action-mask shapes too). Since Phase 4 the trainer is typed by the protocol, and Orbit alone keeps the asymmetric `concat`. GPU noise and multi-rank use are unverified.
- [[kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic|Kaggriculture model joins Isaiah's factory, trunk compile and masked critic]]: Task 3.1 model side puts the model in `ModelConfig` and `create_model` with game-checked specs. It dispatches trunk compile through a nominal `TrunkCompileAPI`, which compiles only the blocks behind `_run_trunk`'s guard, and it masks the winner softmax as Isaiah does. CPU tests only, Codex r1 found no functional defect; `FullConfig` now pairs it with the Task 3.4 `KaggricultureEnvConfig`.
- [[evaluation-and-truncation-follow-the-kaggriculture-objective|Evaluation and truncation follow the Kaggriculture objective]] — Tasks 3.2/3.3: raw-bank evaluation winners, economic reward kept on truncation, joint per-player clipping and value-mode guards, a per-evaluation seed in a checked int64 band (distinct per step within a run, not a global stream separator) and promotion telemetry logged after promotion completes; proven on the trainer seam (CPU TDD, fake env, 1,344 Python passes); since the Task 3.4 merge the guards run through the registered Kaggriculture env config and every `configs/kaggriculture*.yaml`; since Task 1.5 the evaluation env is the seeded native adapter; policy evaluation mapping and a real Kaggriculture run wait for Task 3.1.
- [[kaggriculture-configs-follow-isaiahs-scaling-6m-recipe|Kaggriculture configs follow Isaiah's scaling_6m recipe]] — Task 3.4: 2-rank 128/8, 4-rank 64/4 and 8-rank 32/2 configs deliberately keep scaling_6m's global batch, optimizer, PPO, teacher and compile settings; they load through the real FullConfig with a typed KaggricultureEnvConfig; run_ppo startup checks every forward against the model's GEMM chunking before allocation, prints bounded headroom, then stops explicitly because Task 3.1 rollout storage and action mapping are missing (the native env exists since Task 1.5).

## Phase 4 — teacher

- [[kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce|Kaggriculture teacher distills per-slot KL and per-seat winner CE]]: Phases 4.1–4.3 on CPU. The grammar core gives replay-conditioned per-slot masked logits and a liveness-weighted KL(teacher ‖ student), cached as `KaggricultureTeacherTargets` (102,208 B per seat row) with a grammar signature. The cached path is bit-for-bit the combined path. The model owns a live-seat-mean winner CE, PPO dispatches teacher calls statelessly and logs `teacher/cache_bytes`. Eleven killed mutations. Phase 4 is not complete: the trainer and run_ppo launch/resume tests are written but skipped (the launch/resume pair dry-run with config validation bypassed). After the integration merge an unskipped probe still fails all four on the missing trainer observation mapping and run_ppo's Kaggriculture stop, which since the Tasks 1.4/1.5 merge names only Task 3.1 rollout storage and action mapping (configs and value-mode guards have landed), and 4.4 is not done though its configs prerequisite has merged. A GPU component bundle at `8fde43c` (synthetic, fresh weights, BF16, compiled trunk) found near-zero self KL, bit-identical cached and combined paths and a finite teacher-term backward; cross-chunk/minibatch equality, multi-rank and trainer integration stay open.

## Phase 5 and 7 — BC data and evaluation preparation

- [[rebuild-data-preparation-preserves-replay-identity|Replay identity and data/evaluation preparation]] — Typed engine-independent selector preserves all 252 historical episode IDs and splits; offline source custody, v4 preparation, seed replay export and four compact opponent recommendations carry explicit native/runtime gaps.

## Phase 6 — GPU evidence

- [[compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows|Compiled GEMM template overflows above 2^21 rows]] — Torch 2.9 Inductor max-autotune Triton GEMM templates wrap the 32-bit A-load offset once rows × input width exceeds 2^31 with an int32 size argument (measured at widths 4096/768/512, silent in the real trunk; output-wide GEMMs stayed correct to 2^32); design bound M × max(in, out) for training; trunk guard measured correct at L−1 and rejecting L at `1ddc71d` (the packed path now chunks, CPU-tested; GPU chunk counts timed with a teacher proxy, no correctness check); Task 3.1 registration and guarded trunk compile dispatch are CPU-tested; an A/B found ATEN-only (cuBLAS) GEMMs correct above the bound at +4.5–6.5 % model-only update wall, now required for Kaggriculture compiles (CPU-tested) with the guards kept; a depth-1 real-trunk backward was correct above the bound under ATEN-only (depth 8 and the production backend-claim wiring unmeasured); production compliance unproven.
- [[pod-v3-environment-runs-flash-attn-2-8-3-forward-on-sm120|Pod v3 environment runs flash-attn 2.8.3 forward on sm_120]] — Phase 6.0 venv `/workspace/kg-v3-rebuild` (torch 2.9.0, triton 3.5.0, flash-attn 2.8.3 prebuilt wheel with sm_120 cubins); varlen kernel's max error against fp32 SDPA equals BF16 SDPA's (0.00359), and the packed flash path runs in eager and compiled trunk forwards. Forward only, trunk numerics unqualified; wheel digest outside `uv.lock` and possibly shared hard-linked venv files are hazards. Codex-approved.
- [[model-only-sps-ceiling-bounds-per-rank-throughput|Model-only SPS ceiling bounds per-rank throughput]] — Conditional component estimate, not end-to-end SPS: 2,085 / 1,757 / 957 model-only env steps/s per rank (sparse / mid / dense) on a synthetic update schedule at `e1458d2`; engine budget 53–116 µs per env step for ≤ 10 % loss; allocated peak 40.3 GiB, reserved 85.0 GiB unexplained. Not rankable. Codex-approved.

## Cross-cutting

- [[starter-history-and-knowledge-remain-retrievable|Starter history and knowledge remain retrievable]] — The Isaiah source history/license, redirected remotes and selective cookbook lifecycle are retained with explicit verification limits.

## Reference branch (historical)

Since the [[../decisions/restart-the-port-from-isaiahs-clean-base|restart]], the following References describe the implementation on branch `kg/reference-2026-09-29` (tag `kg-reference-2026-09-29`), not the current tree. Use them as reference for the rebuild.

- [[full-turn-intentions-coordinate-batched-action-heads|Full-turn intentions coordinate batched action heads]] — Optional U/A hypothesis; Isaiah and the current model already retain shared scratch/plan context. No demonstrated need or cost-benefit for a dedicated coordinator.
- [[shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop|Shared PPO adapts game batches without a second loop]] — One shared Isaiah PPO trainer carries Kaggriculture batches; its core is upstream-equivalent, the recipe is partially aligned, and teacher, cadence, CUDA-fault and GPU-qualification gaps are tracked in ops. Historical SPS measurements link to their receipts.
- [[explicit-game-tokens-and-grammar-replace-orbit-heads|Explicit game tokens and grammar replace Orbit heads]] — Restored player token and entity/player/plan batched heads pass local checks; checkpoint schema changes explicitly, while prior GPU results retain their old-model scope.
- [[bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads|Native replay BC bootstrap]] — Market-disabled controls preserve3000 bank; exact admitted replay actions and Rust features support separate current-model BC, with episode holdout, two-rank smoke, observed overfitting and incomplete quality validation; automatic PPO disabled; BC stopped early for a separately requested PPO experiment, which then failed with a CUDA illegal memory access later traced to a compiler GEMM overflow; the planned architecture alignment schedules one BC rerun. Source review corrects omitted-unit handling: Python None is rejected, not encoded as NONE.

