cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:11:# Kaggriculture model joins Isaiah's factory, trunk compile and masked critic
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:13:Branch `kg/rebuild-trainer-model`, based on `kg/isaiah-gap-closure` at `e1458d2`. The [[kaggriculture-encoder-reuses-isaiah-stateless-layers|encoder]] and [[kaggriculture-grammar-heads-sit-behind-isaiahs-actor-projection|heads]] References left three items open: shared registration, trainer compile wiring, and the critic's masked softmax. This note records all three.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:21:- **Trunk compile.**
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:22:  - `TrunkCompileAPI` (`python/owl/model/base.py`) is a nominal ABC with `compile_transformer_trunk(*, mode) -> int`. `StatelessTransformerV1` and `KaggricultureTransformer` both implement it.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:23:  - `configure_model_compile` accepts any `nn.Module`. For `trunk` it dispatches with `isinstance` (no `getattr`). The recurrent model keeps Isaiah's specific error, and any other model raises.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:24:  - Kaggriculture compiles only `_forward_transformer_trunk` (blocks plus `final_norm`). `_run_trunk` calls it after the overflow guard and chunking.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:25:  - `mlp` compiles `blocks[i].mlp` in place, and those modules run only inside `_run_trunk`.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:41:- `tests/kaggriculture/test_model_compile.py` (11 tests):
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:42:  - the trunk target compiles exactly the bound `_forward_transformer_trunk` with `dynamic=True`
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:43:  - over sampling, replay and value calls, only block submodules and `final_norm` run inside the compiled region. Stems, critic, actor projection and heads run outside it.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:44:  - the compiled callable is called once per chunk, and the guard raises before it runs
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:45:  - `mlp` compiles exactly the block MLPs, and they run only inside `_run_trunk`
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:46:  - no target compiles the whole model
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:47:  - an AST pin lists every compile call site on the trainer and model paths
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:48:  - Against the base dispatch, 4 of these fail (`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/trainer-model/compile-red.log`).
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:55:- Codex verification r1 (`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/codex/verify-3.1-rest-r1.md`, evidence in `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/codex/verify-3.1-rest/`): APPROVE WITH EDITS, no functional defect. It reran pytest (1,324 passed, 4 skipped), Isaiah's suites (1,048 passed, 3 skipped) and mypy, and two mutations (compile-guard bypass, unmasked critic) failed their intended tests. Its two wording findings are applied here.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:56:- Codex verification r2 (`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/codex/verify-3.1-rest-r2.md`): APPROVE WITH EDITS, no functional defect or shim wrapper; both r1 findings resolved. It reran pytest (1,324 passed, 4 skipped), Isaiah's suites (1,048 passed, 3 skipped), mypy (57 files) and the same two mutations. Its one finding, a stale current-state claim in the [[compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows|compiled-GEMM Reference]], is fixed there.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:60:- Nothing here runs a real `torch.compile` or CUDA. Every compile test uses a recording stand-in, so Inductor graph breaks, recompiles and the flash path in the compiled trunk remain Phase 6 GPU qualification.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:61:- The trainer cannot build this model yet. `FullConfig` now loads it with `KaggricultureEnvConfig` (see the [[kaggriculture-configs-follow-isaiahs-scaling-6m-recipe|configs Reference]]), but `run_ppo` stops at its explicit Kaggriculture guard because rollout storage and the Kaggriculture observation/action mapping (rest of Task 3.1) are open; the native env and Python adapter exist since the Tasks 1.4/1.5 merge.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:4:description: "Phases 4.1-4.3 on CPU: replay-conditioned per-slot masked logits and a liveness-weighted per-slot KL(teacher || student), cached as KaggricultureTeacherTargets (102,208 B per seat row) with a grammar signature, a cached path bit-for-bit equal to the combined path, a live-seat-mean winner CE owned by the model, stateless PPO teacher dispatch and teacher/cache_bytes; eleven killed mutations. Phase 4 is not complete: the trainer and run_ppo launch/resume tests are written but skipped (the launch/resume pair dry-run with config validation bypassed); after the integration merge an unskipped probe still fails all four on the missing Task 3.1 trainer observation mapping and run_ppo's Kaggriculture stop, which since the Tasks 1.4/1.5 merge names only Task 3.1 rollout storage and action mapping (configs and value-mode guards have landed), and 4.4 is not done though its configs prerequisite has merged. A later GPU component bundle at 8fde43c (synthetic inputs, fresh weights, BF16 and compiled trunk) found self KL near zero, perturbed KL positive, cached and combined paths bit-identical and a finite teacher-term loss backward, and timed target precompute; cross-chunk/minibatch equality, multi-rank and full trainer integration stay open."
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce.md:88:The estimator is Isaiah's: teacher-forced conditionals at the behavior policy's replayed prefix, summed per slot, not an unbiased joint-program KL. Both sides must share the grammar tables and `hire_limit`; replay admission does not detect a mismatch that still admits the program.
