cookbook/references/kaggriculture-configs-follow-isaiahs-scaling-6m-recipe.md:28:  - `python/owl/kaggriculture/config.py` adds `KaggricultureEnvConfig` (`n_envs`, the Kaggriculture obs/action specs, `reward_mode: win_loss` only, `reward_shaping`, `pin_memory`, `native_threads ≥ 1`; Isaiah's `two_player_weight` is an unknown key) and, in Task 3.4, a `KaggricultureRewardConfig` with the reference branch's field names and defaults. Since Task 1.5 the single definition is `owl.kaggriculture.rewards.KaggricultureRewardConfig`: all six coefficients are required, finite and nonnegative (no defaults), enabled caps must sum strictly below one, positive `econ_shaping` needs a positive `econ_cap` and a positive binary64 product with the starvation or drought weight, and a positive ineffective weight needs a positive ineffective cap (see the [[reward-reuse-preserves-objective-and-critic-semantics|reward Reference]]). The shipped YAML files set all six explicitly (`econ_ineffective_cap` 0.1 in every ranked config).
